WEBVTT

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:22.030
Who are you?

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:31.420
"One of the voices
Always angelic

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:34.470
It is about me,
Sharply expresses itself:

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:37.180
Those thousand questions
Spreading their roots

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:39.350
Bring in the end,
Only drunkenness and madness;

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:40.100
Understand this trick. So gay, so easy:

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.560
Is she with you?
Understand this trick. So gay, so easy:

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:45.730
It is only wave, only flower,
And that is your family!

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:50.860
And then a voice
- How angelic it is! -"

00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:40.740
Hey, Eric, is there any activity in the--

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:43.950
Wh-What?

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:47.700
Hey, quit shoving! Ow!

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:49.670
What are you--

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:53.960
G-Genie,
did you ever get your license renewed?

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.250
Hey, where are you going?

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:10.760
There's no other way.

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:13.520
Hey, what are you saying?
We can't do that!

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:15.020
Then, what should we do?

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:18.360
Everyone, please remain calm!

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:22.200
At this time, the Royal Police's
hazardous material disposal team

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:26.040
is dealing with the situation,
so please be patient a while longer!

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:28.710
That's all you keep saying!

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:30.830
Tell us what's going on!

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:35.290
What do we do?

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:39.880
Even if you ask, there's not much
we can do in this situation.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:42.380
Officers, everything will be okay, right?

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:46.970
Ugly. This is so ugly.

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:50.140
Death is drawing closer,
and this is how they act?

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:52.810
I'm not like you people.

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:54.690
I'm special!

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:59.110
I will go down in history
as the very embodiment of terror!

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:01.950
I embrace my death with dignity and pride!

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:08.660
No finesse.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:10.830
His code is slapped together.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.330
Technical skill, one.

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:13.960
Specs are plagiarized.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.170
A lazy imitation.

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:17.250
Originality, zero.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:21.510
Offensive and defensive capability,
both one. Grade, D.

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:26.630
A third rate hack of a malware writer,
huh? How unimpressive.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:27.810
Which means...

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:31.810
2,700 seconds remaining.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:35.230
I could beat him three times over
with time to spare.

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:11.350
"It is about me,
Sharply expresses itself:

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:15.980
And sings at this moment
Like a sister to breath:

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:18.810
With a German tone,
But ardent and full:

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:24.360
The world is vicious;
If that surprises you!"

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:43.000
The king has landed.

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:45.960
I'll have my audience
at his father's grave.

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:25.380
Hey, this is bad!

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.300
No way! Crap!

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:33.890
Understood. The black swan
has taken flight as planned, then.

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:37.930
In that case,
I'll have the clowns make their exit.

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:42.060
Hey! If this keeps up,
I'm gonna get skunked!

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:44.730
Can I wrap this up already?

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:48.150
Whoever this is, he's the real deal!

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:51.200
We have to get ready to run!
Are you listening?

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:59.580
If you can't detect danger,
you've deteriorated as a living creature.

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:01.410
Bye-bye.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.010
It's stopped.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:18.020
The counterattack attempts have stopped.

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:21.520
Is he giving up now that he's losing?

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:25.190
No, this guy doesn't pay
that much attention to detail.

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:28.650
Maybe it's a trap to lure us
into the building,

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:32.780
or maybe a tactic to confuse us
and slow us down,

00:06:33.230 --> 00:06:36.820
or maybe they didn't plan
for this situation.

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:40.040
So it's sink or swim time.

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:43.870
Either way,
we have no options and no way out.

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:46.090
We'll take the bait and deal with it.

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:48.550
Jean, connect me to the hazmat team.

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:49.800
On it.

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:10.020
It's open!

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:10.860
We're saved!
It's open!

00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:12.440
They're coming out!

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:13.820
Call it in!
They're coming out!

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:20.910
Eric, it's from Kaela.

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:22.540
Put her on speaker.

00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:28.100
Eric?

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:30.710
Kaela, it's Eric. You're on speaker.

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:34.090
I'm with Jean, Abbot, and Brody.

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:36.510
If that's okay, go ahead.

00:07:37.090 --> 00:07:39.970
I have the building's systems back online.

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:43.440
Well done. Now please get back
to locating the poison--

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:46.520
Already on it.
But something's bugging me.

00:07:46.970 --> 00:07:47.940
What is it?

00:07:48.770 --> 00:07:50.770
While I was attacking the system,

00:07:50.770 --> 00:07:54.360
there were repeated defensive attempts
from the criminals.

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:56.660
But then they suddenly stopped.

00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:57.950
Stopped?

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:01.620
Is it a trap?

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:21.810
It's the gas!

00:08:22.470 --> 00:08:23.470
Run!

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:33.610
Mario! Sit-rep!

00:08:34.730 --> 00:08:36.360
Talk to me! Anybody!

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:38.410
Brandon! Lily!

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:40.450
Somebody respond!

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:45.540
How could this happen?

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:46.870
Damn it.

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:49.000
Kaela!

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:53.460
If you manipulate the HVAC system
and direct the flow of air,

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:57.430
the gas will be diverted
to empty parts of the building! Do it!

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:01.390
That risks depriving any airtight rooms
of oxygen.

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:03.380
If anyone's in one, they'll-

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:05.050
The gas is what's important!

00:09:05.050 --> 00:09:07.350
I'll take responsibility! There's no time!

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:08.680
Hurry!

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:09.560
Roger that.

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:25.290
Zeppole di ...seppe.

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:42.930
Boris! Where are you? Is Keith with you?

00:09:45.090 --> 00:09:48.060
He is! We're northbound on route 8!

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:50.640
Route 8? What are you doing out there?

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:53.690
I don't know! Ask Keith!

00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:06.080
Keith, we have an emergency!
Get back here right away!

00:10:07.070 --> 00:10:09.370
The gas was released in the tower!

00:10:10.490 --> 00:10:12.240
Wh-What did you say?

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:16.000
We're currently unable to raise
any of our people inside!

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:17.620
Genie, head back!

00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:18.930
There's nothing to worry about.

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:22.930
Sorry, Eric. You handle it.

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:26.390
What are you saying, you idiot?
Lily and the others are--

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:28.100
If it's been released...

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:32.690
If it's been released, the gas is fake.

00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:35.280
A dispersal meant to cause chaos.

00:10:35.810 --> 00:10:39.570
A simple ploy to buy time.
Probably to cover their escape.

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:40.740
Based on what?

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:44.240
Didn't you see it?
The criminal is a myopic thinker.

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:45.950
An immature narcissist.

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:50.790
Basically, a dumb, self-absorbed kid,
obsessed with superficial aesthetics.

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:52.580
That's a mean way to put it.

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:57.420
In a narcissist's autobiography,
his own death is a crucial component.

00:10:58.370 --> 00:11:03.390
Writhing in pain, slowly dying as his skin
blisters from a modified corrosive gas...

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:06.590
You think they would be okay with that?

00:11:06.590 --> 00:11:10.140
Go though all the old profiles again.
That doesn't happen.

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:15.060
You might be right,
but what you're saying is just theory.

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:18.730
What's a fact is
we can't raise anyone inside.

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:21.820
It's a knockout gas, then. Listen, Eric.

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:26.200
This incident and the IFV theft
have the same structure:

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:28.490
Under cover of all the chaos,

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:31.910
a sophisticated mind is working
towards some other objective.

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:33.370
In other words,

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:38.840
a group is using crimes of opportunity
to carry out their own planned crimes.

00:11:39.330 --> 00:11:42.220
They might even be
deliberately manipulating crimes

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:44.340
that appear to be random occurrences.

00:11:45.090 --> 00:11:47.680
A cycle of madness is about to break out.

00:11:48.670 --> 00:11:53.140
The answer won't be found on the surface.
It's always behind the scenes.

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:00.520
You're late.

00:12:00.980 --> 00:12:03.990
Kamui got hung up making his stupid trash.

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:06.570
They're ecstatic.

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:11.780
They were able to end their pathetic lives
as part of one of my works.

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:15.710
Meaning they were pathetic
to the very end, huh?

00:12:16.410 --> 00:12:19.750
Kamui, you haven't forgotten
our objective, I trust?

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:23.040
Of course not.
That was just part of a side project.

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:25.800
We accomplished the objective just fine.

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:31.010
And yet he isn't here with us.

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:34.220
You're intentionally
misinterpreting my orders.

00:12:34.470 --> 00:12:36.100
That's a bad habit.

00:12:36.430 --> 00:12:37.480
Yeah, yeah.

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:42.650
Minatsuki, do we really have to bring
the black-winged king back with us?

00:12:43.190 --> 00:12:45.650
Yes, because those are our orders.

00:12:46.230 --> 00:12:48.490
Does he have to be alive?

00:12:55.070 --> 00:12:57.000
He only needs to be alive.

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:12.640
Welcome to Divine Days.

00:13:13.880 --> 00:13:18.400
For a few days every October, Lake Lenan
becomes a gateway to the kingdom of God.

00:13:19.350 --> 00:13:22.020
Souls dance with joy in the darkness.

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:34.070
Don't you think it's pretty?
Countless lights in the darkness...

00:13:35.320 --> 00:13:37.040
I love this place.

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:43.300
One little light can be enough to keep you
from fearing the dark or losing your way.

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:46.130
Do you get what I'm trying to say?

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:49.210
Light represents hope.

00:13:49.210 --> 00:13:51.760
I don't want to hear your nonsense.

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:53.140
Where is she?

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:55.680
If you don't answer me, I'll kill you!

00:13:56.720 --> 00:13:58.690
You're so easy to figure out.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:01.690
Is she your light?

00:14:02.220 --> 00:14:04.900
Your memories of her are vague,
aren't they?

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:08.700
Oh, I know. You don't even know
very much about yourself.

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:13.030
That's why you're shouting so desperately.
I can hear it.

00:14:13.690 --> 00:14:17.040
"I'm here! I'm right here!

00:14:17.610 --> 00:14:18.790
I'm alive!

00:14:19.240 --> 00:14:21.080
Somebody find me!"

00:14:31.670 --> 00:14:35.720
Unfortunately, all that's here
are the spirits of the dead and us.

00:14:36.970 --> 00:14:41.730
Out of all of us, I'm the only one
who spent time with you, however briefly.

00:14:41.970 --> 00:14:44.440
There was even a time
when I lived for you.

00:14:46.350 --> 00:14:48.820
We even watched these lights together.

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:53.320
That's why I lured you here.
To make you remember.

00:15:06.830 --> 00:15:12.470
Oh, dear.
My fragile hopes have been dashed.

00:15:14.550 --> 00:15:19.430
I've been thinking. About who it was
who locked away your memories.

00:15:29.310 --> 00:15:31.150
And I finally figured it out.

00:15:34.270 --> 00:15:36.030
Where is she?

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:43.290
The one who locked away your memories
was none other than...

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:45.540
you yourself.

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:49.540
You wanted to forget it all, I bet.

00:15:50.500 --> 00:15:53.090
Everything that happened that day.

00:15:53.880 --> 00:15:55.220
All of it.

00:15:57.340 --> 00:15:58.340
But...

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:04.430
I won't let you forget about me.

00:16:06.180 --> 00:16:10.990
I'll never forgive you
for not choosing me!

00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:17.450
-Where are we?
-Like I know!

00:16:19.990 --> 00:16:22.460
So, how about filling me in?

00:16:23.030 --> 00:16:25.620
What are we chasing after?

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:27.960
I'm not sure.

00:16:29.870 --> 00:16:32.170
It's something I need to chase down.

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:35.340
So, what is that?

00:16:36.750 --> 00:16:38.970
I wish I knew, too.

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:50.630
Cut off my left leg.
It'll be useful to you someday.

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:56.040
Touch Canopus.

00:17:58.250 --> 00:17:59.550
If you do that...

00:18:01.710 --> 00:18:02.880
Canopus?

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:15.690
Do you know your name?

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:19.320
Zeppole... di San Giuseppe.

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:20.990
Do you know where you are?

00:18:22.360 --> 00:18:23.950
Where...

00:18:34.220 --> 00:18:36.250
Please don't sit up so quickly!

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:39.300
Are you queasy,
or experiencing any discomfort?

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:40.420
How?

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:44.050
I saw gas flood into the room, and...

00:18:44.260 --> 00:18:46.340
They say it was just knockout gas.

00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:49.440
They sure got us this time.

00:18:50.890 --> 00:18:54.560
So our perp was bluffing all along?

00:18:55.640 --> 00:18:58.820
Well, that doesn't seem to be the case,
either.

00:18:59.440 --> 00:19:00.360
What do you mean?

00:19:02.070 --> 00:19:06.450
They did find real gas.
They just didn't use it.

00:19:06.860 --> 00:19:07.870
But, well...

00:19:09.950 --> 00:19:12.750
The way they found it wasn't normal.

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:34.270
Looks like we just missed them.

00:19:38.560 --> 00:19:45.150
BLUE OXIDIZED COATING

00:19:49.990 --> 00:19:54.170
They found the remains of the criminals,
other than their skins.

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:55.080
Where?

00:19:55.080 --> 00:19:57.750
Um, maybe you'd be better off not knowing.

00:19:57.750 --> 00:20:01.090
If you knew,
you wouldn't be able to eat for a while.

00:20:02.580 --> 00:20:05.590
I've been sensing something
for a while now.

00:20:08.090 --> 00:20:11.260
Don't these cases lately
seem strange to you?

00:20:12.180 --> 00:20:16.430
I mean, none of these incidents
have been resolved.

00:20:17.810 --> 00:20:21.270
I feel like something is going on
in this city.

00:20:21.980 --> 00:20:25.860
You get all serious for once,
and it's about that?

00:20:27.030 --> 00:20:29.660
I think your gut is right.

00:20:30.070 --> 00:20:31.410
It is, isn't it?

00:20:32.530 --> 00:20:35.630
Though with me,
my "gut" is usually misleading.

00:20:36.030 --> 00:20:39.200
You're right, though.
Something's going on.

00:20:39.200 --> 00:20:41.300
If we know that, then why don't we--

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:45.590
"I shall faithfully uphold the
constitution of the Kingdom of Cremona,

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:49.550
comply with our king's orders,
prioritize my duties as a law officer,

00:20:49.550 --> 00:20:51.970
and demand that they be obeyed."

00:20:54.340 --> 00:20:57.310
"With favor towards none,
with fear towards none,

00:20:57.310 --> 00:21:00.800
with hatred towards none,
obeying the dictates of my conscience,

00:21:02.500 --> 00:21:06.570
to safeguard the kingdom, as well as
the freedom and rights of her citizens,

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:10.860
I solemnly swear to carry out my duties
as an officer of the law!"

00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:16.950
The day we took that oath,
we became cops. You and me.

00:21:18.080 --> 00:21:22.000
We just need to solve cases
as they come in, one at a time.

00:21:22.330 --> 00:21:24.220
More like, that's all we can do.

00:21:26.210 --> 00:21:29.470
But as those wins add up,
small as they are,

00:21:29.960 --> 00:21:32.400
it will eventually grow into a clue
that points us to something.

00:21:32.400 --> 00:21:33.800
It's a perfect world we longing for
it will eventually grow into a clue
that points us to something.

00:21:33.800 --> 00:21:34.220
It's a perfect world we longing for

00:21:34.220 --> 00:21:35.850
That's what I believe.
It's a perfect world we longing for

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:36.400
It's a perfect world we longing for

00:21:36.890 --> 00:21:41.810
That said, I have no idea in hell what
that "something" is right now, though.

00:21:43.690 --> 00:21:44.610
I guess not.

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:48.360
So, thinking about all that other stuff
is pointless.

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:51.080
Right?

00:21:53.610 --> 00:21:54.580
Understood!

00:21:55.070 --> 00:21:57.540
I'll stop thinking!

00:21:59.240 --> 00:22:01.160
No! He didn't mean entirely!

00:22:06.550 --> 00:22:10.390
Cursed shadows haunt and gather

00:22:10.390 --> 00:22:14.010
In the city of no answer

00:22:14.390 --> 00:22:18.310
as we follow endless questions

00:22:18.310 --> 00:22:22.230
hands up in the same reflection

00:22:22.520 --> 00:22:26.150
just used to be
Sometimes we try to feel how things

00:22:26.150 --> 00:22:30.280
in yesterdays

00:22:30.570 --> 00:22:34.370
No one ever make it better, no one ever lives forever

00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:37.750
Wake me up and let me go

00:22:38.160 --> 00:22:45.960
Someday I’ll be gone

00:22:45.960 --> 00:22:52.050
To somewhere we all belong

00:22:52.050 --> 00:22:54.800
For so long
